# Image gate: what `docker build` copies out of the Cloud Build source into the
# image. .gcloudignore is the secrecy authority one step upstream; this file
# repeats those exclusions and then drops what the *image* has no use for —
# infra, docs, operator scripts and tests are legitimate build-context content
# that `next build` never reads.
#
# Note: these are Docker patterns, not gitignore patterns — a bare name matches
# only at the context root, so anything that must match at any depth is
# written with a leading **/.

# --- Everything .gcloudignore withholds, repeated so a local `docker build`
# --- (which never sees .gcloudignore) is just as tight. -------------------
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*service-account*.json
**/.firebase
.claude
scratch
.scratch*
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*-debug.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/.pnpm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/node_modules
.next
out
build
terraform
docs
# The feedback tracker's screenshots are runtime files of the admin-only
# route app/api/admin/feedback/screenshots/[name] (ROADMAP N73; traced into
# the standalone output by next.config.ts). Keep in step with .gcloudignore.
!docs/feedback/screenshots/*.png
**/*.md
**/*.pdf

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore

# --- Pipeline plumbing: read by gcloud/Docker outside the image ------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gcloudignore
cloudbuild.yaml

# --- Operator tooling: run from a laptop, never from the container ---------
scripts

# --- Separately deployed Cloud Functions package. tsconfig.json excludes
# --- functions/, so `next build` never type-checks or bundles it.
functions
firebase.json
firestore.rules
firestore.indexes.json

# --- Tests. Nothing under app/, components/ or lib/ imports a test file or
# --- the fake-Firestore helper, so `next build`'s type-check is unaffected.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
lib/test-support
